<ArticleLayout
  title="Responsible Mining & Digital Governance"
  description="MineralsReady: a digital compliance and training platform for artisanal mining and government readiness, in Sierra Leone, Nigeria and Zimbabwe."
>
  <p>
    Artisanal mining is a major source of livelihoods across the
    countries we work in, and a sector where formal compliance and
    everyday practice often sit far apart. This area works on closing
    that gap with a digital tool built for the purpose.
  </p>

  <h2>What this covers</h2>
  <p>
    MineralsReady is a digital compliance and training platform,
    developed with a university research partner, that supports
    artisanal and small-scale mining operators and government bodies in
    building genuine readiness for responsible sourcing standards.
    Pilots are underway or in development in Sierra Leone, Nigeria and
    Zimbabwe.
  </p>
  <p>
    The platform combines research-backed content design with a
    practical field-implementation interface, so the tool reflects how
    an ASM site and a government regulator actually work, not only how
    a policy document describes them.
  </p>

  <h2>How this connects</h2>
  <p>
    This programme sits close to the work of Orivia Minerals Hub, our
    sister initiative focused specifically on artisanal and small-scale
    mining across frontier markets. Where Ayara&rsquo;s role centres on
    the research, training-platform and governance-readiness side,
    Orivia brings direct ASM operating experience and sector-specific
    advisory.
  </p>
</ArticleLayout>
